// This strategy tracks three pieces of state across decoding: the full emitted
// answer in generated, whether we are currently inside a math-computation span
// delimited by << and >>, and the contents of that active constrained span in
// currentConstrainedOut. Outside a span, generation is mostly free, but if the
// model strongly favors a token containing "<<" or directly emits the delimiter
// token "<<", we open a constrained span so arithmetic text can be checked by
// the parser. Inside a span, we first try a cheap speculative argmax when it is
// parser-valid; otherwise we fall back to ConstrainedStep, and once the parser
// reports a complete constrained prefix we close with >>. This tracked suffix
